> Retain the original event dates and forty-year view

The original events are Apollo 11's landing date, 1969-07-20; the US
Declaration date, 1776-07-04; and Christmas,2025-12-25. The original
Sunday/Thursday/Thursday results are retained. These are calendar
calculations on supplied civil dates, without interpreting event times,
locations or timezones. The same program checks every first-of-month
in 2025 against Zeller's independent congruence.

Zeller uses Saturday=0, Sunday=1, …, Friday=6, so the conversion to
Doomsday's Sunday-first code is (h+6) mod 7. Comparing raw codes would
be a mistake. The original 2000–2039 annual-anchor scatter is retained
with named weekday ticks and a separate colour for leap years. Weekday
codes wrap after Saturday; an apparent downward jump is modular wrap,
not a backwards-moving calendar.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/doomsday_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  struct Event {const char* name; int year,month,day;};
  std::print("| event | date | weekday |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n");
  for(const auto e:std::vector<Event>{{"Apollo 11 Moon landing",1969,7,20},{"US Declaration of Independence",1776,7,4},{"Christmas Day 2025",2025,12,25}})
    std::print("| {} | {}-{:02}-{:02} | {} |\n",e.name,e.year,e.month,e.day,dm::algorithms::doomsday_day_name(dm::algorithms::doomsday_weekday(e.year,e.month,e.day)));
  std::print("\n| month of 2025 | Doomsday code on day 1 | converted Zeller code | weekday |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | :--- |\n");
  int agree=0;
  for(int m=1;m<=12;++m) {
    const int a=dm::algorithms::doomsday_weekday(2025,m,1);
    const int b=(dm::algorithms::zeller_gregorian(2025,m,1)+6)%7;
    agree+=a==b;
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",m,a,b,dm::algorithms::doomsday_day_name(a));
  }
  std::print("\nDoomsday == converted Zeller on 2025 month starts: {}/12.\n",agree);
  std::vector<double> ordinary_year,ordinary_day,leap_year,leap_day;
  for(int y=2000;y<=2039;++y) {
    const auto t=dm::algorithms::doomsday_year_trace(y);
    (t.leap?leap_year:ordinary_year).push_back(y);
    (t.leap?leap_day:ordinary_day).push_back(t.doomsday);
  }
  auto p=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.points(ordinary_year,ordinary_day,"ordinary",{37,99,235},5)
   .points(leap_year,leap_day,"leap",{217,119,6},6)
   .y_ticks({0,1,2,3,4,5,6},{"Sun","Mon","Tue","Wed","Thu","Fri","Sat"})
   .title("Original annual Doomsdays, 2000–2039").x_label("year")
   .y_label("weekday of February's last day").y_limits(-.5,8.5)
   .size(1100,570).save_svg("build/doomsday_original.svg");
}
```
